// check: accepted
// CROWN — the sound dual: a handler whose state init performs NOTHING
// installs freely under `with !E`. Charging the init's row must not charge
// an init that has none, which is what keeps every handler in the wheel
// installable — all of theirs are pure, which is exactly why no gate saw
// the leak until one was written.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect F { g() -> Int }
handler hf with s = 1 {
  g() => resume(s),
}
fn good() with !E = (g()) ~> hf
fn main() = good()
